	(text "Mean Well NID100-SPEC (2024-10-30): EMC circuit C1/C2 120 uF/63 V, L1 15 uH (NiZn), C3 22 uF/35 V; ext. C max 100 uF/16 V;\n  fuse recommended 8 A; R.C.: on = open or 1.2-12 V, off = < 0.4 V; pin 12 \"Trim (optional)\", no formula published.\nL1 is a single winding in +Vin: the input return is the common board ground (non-isolated NID, amp on the same ground).\nExternal C on +5V: C7 22 uF + C8 10 uF (X7R 1206, ~70 % at 5 V) + C9 + C10 + LDO input path (behind 2.2 Ohm)  ~ 35 uF << 100 uF.\nPi output: 0453010.MR -> LK1 (wire link) -> USB4105 VBUS; CC1/CC2 Rp 10 k to 5 V (3 A); Pi uses PSU_MAX_CURRENT=5000.\nBench 2.7 test pads: 5V (NID out) | 5V_F (after fuse) | EXT5V (at USB4105) ; LK1 opened for the series current.\nTrim network DNP (D23/V20): R8 Trim->Com raises Vout, R9 Trim->+Vout lowers it (FB-divider convention, not published\n  by Mean Well). Spec lists pin 12 as \"Trim (optional)\" with no formula; on arrival measure R(pin 12-Com) unpowered and\n  Vout with a trimmer clipped from TP13 to GND before fitting R8. No response at pin 12 -> alternative-regulator decision."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f89971f1-e453-44ba-9cbb-1aa183040ec7")
	)
